{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>and Gashmu said</b> — he is Geshem the Arab, and the vav is added, like the other instances of extra vav." "<b>and you are to be</b> — he means he wants you to be king over them." "<b>according to these things</b> — he explained: a matter he sent to me, or he explained: according to these things I have heard."], :book :nehemiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites the ketiv גשם (Geshem) against the qere/parallel גשמו (Gashmu); 'the other instances' refers to standard cases of extraneous vav in biblical names."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nehemiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nechemya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:10.891514405Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}